Subject: [PATCH 08857/11362] The 0.09-vs-0.12 gap is not a regression: the
 baselines ran a different stack entirely

Checked the actual config behind the 0.12/0.08 baseline submissions via the
preserved pre-2026-07-31-restage snapshot: they ran Qwen3.5-9B-MTP on a
single NvidiaL4 (24GB), not gemma-4-31B on RTX Pro 6000. The 2026-07-28
model migration sits between those baselines and today's submission, and no
submission in between used a correctly-configured kernel -- today's 0.09 is
the first clean data point for the current stack, not a second measurement
of a known-good one. Real open question this surfaces: ARC-AGI-3 scoring is
efficiency-weighted with a hard wall-clock cap, so a larger/slower model
could plausibly score lower end-to-end even with better per-decision
induction quality (the migration's own evidence measured offline induction
accuracy only). Not resolved -- would need n=2+ submissions on the current
stack to know if 0.09 is representative.

